      ],
      "source": "https://www.riovista.org/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After floods in 1861–62, the town relocated to higher ground, establishing the present Rio Vista.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.riovista.org/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Rio Vista Bridge, a drawbridge designed by Joseph Strauss—the Golden Gate Bridge architect—stands as a regional landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.riovista.org/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1951 Rio Vista became California’s first city to fluoridate its water supply.",
